Room: Crashpad uploads to the user's own collector.

An unbranded Chromium build starts Crashpad's handler with an empty upload
URL (CrashReporterClient::GetUploadUrl returns kDefaultUploadURL only for
GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING && OFFICIAL_BUILD), so Room wrote minidumps and never
sent one. Room's crash reports go to a collector its user deploys
(B-105, research/notes/crash-reporting.md; the user, 2026-11-01): //room
returns that collector's minidump URL here, from the host's configuration,
before ChromeMain. Consent stays Crashpad's own setting, switched by //room
through crash_reporter::SetUploadConsent when the user opts in or out; with
no URL nothing can upload whatever the consent says.

Phase 6.3, 2026-11-02. //room: room/core/room_application.mm.
diff --git a/components/crash/core/app/crash_reporter_client.cc b/components/crash/core/app/crash_reporter_client.cc
index 0941e78cef594..c25fa613dc458 100644
--- a/components/crash/core/app/crash_reporter_client.cc
+++ b/components/crash/core/app/crash_reporter_client.cc
@@ -140,7 +140,17 @@ void CrashReporterClient::GetSanitizationInformation(
 }
 #endif
 
+namespace room {
+// Room: set by //room/core before ChromeMain. The upload URL of the crash
+// collector Room's user deploys (empty: Crashpad never uploads, as in any
+// unbranded build).
+std::string (*g_crash_upload_url_hook)() = nullptr;
+}  // namespace room
+
 std::string CrashReporterClient::GetUploadUrl() {
+  if (room::g_crash_upload_url_hook) {
+    return room::g_crash_upload_url_hook();
+  }
 #if BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING) && defined(OFFICIAL_BUILD)
   return kDefaultUploadURL;
 #else
